card.statement:
Two $k$-linear maps

\begin{equation}
\mc F: U\times\dots\times U\to V,\qquad\mc G: U'\times\dots\times U'\to V'
\end{equation}

with $k\ge 2$ over a field $\ff$ are

- equivalent if
there exist linear bijections $\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_k:U\to U'$ and
$\psi:V\to V'$ such that

\begin{equation}
\forall u_1,\dots,u_k\in U:\ \mc G(\varphi_1u_1,
\dots,\varphi_ku_k )=\psi \mc F(u_1,\dots,u_k),
\end{equation}

which means that the diagram

\[
\xymatrix@C=30pt{
U\ar[d]_{\varphi_1}
\ar@{}[r]|{\hspace{-25pt}
{\displaystyle\times\dots\times}
\hspace{-25pt}}
&U\ar[d]_{\varphi_k}
\ar[rr]^{\mc F}&&V
\ar[d]_{\psi}
\\
U'\ar@{}[r]|{\hspace{-25pt}
{\displaystyle\times\dots\times}
\hspace{-25pt}}
&U'\ar[rr]^{\mc G}&&V'
}
\]

is commutative;

-
symmetrically equivalent
if there exist linear bijections $\varphi_1,\dots,\varphi_k:U\to U'$ and
$\psi:V\to V'$ such that

\begin{equation}
\forall \sigma \in S_k,\, u_1,\dots,u_k\in U:\ \mc G(\varphi_{\sigma(1)}u_1,
\dots,\varphi_{\sigma(k)}u_k )=\psi \mc F(u_1,\dots,u_k),
\end{equation}

in which $S_k$ is the permutation group;

- congruent if
there exist linear bijections $\varphi:U\to U'$ and
$\psi:V\to V'$ such that

\begin{equation}
\forall u_1,\dots,u_k\in U:\ \mc G(\varphi u_1,
\dots,\varphi u_k )=\psi \mc F(u_1,\dots,u_k).
\end{equation}
